WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.810
Some things I've built.

2
00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:03.350
Some I've led.

3
00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:04.760
NeuRace.

4
00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:06.950
A company I founded and led.

5
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.640
I built the sensor hardware and
the machine-learning software,

6
00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:14.210
then ran it as a service with
professional Grand Prix teams.

7
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:18.450
The driver's brain and body signals,
next to the car's telemetry,

8
00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:21.750
so a team could see how a
driver responded on track.

9
00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:24.530
BrightStory is a startup I co-founded.

10
00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:28.760
It makes personalized visual stories
that help neurodivergent kids,

11
00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:32.110
and their families, get ready
for something unfamiliar.

12
00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:36.350
Bravely is close to that, for children
with cancer and their families.

13
00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:38.970
It helps them understand
what to expect.

14
00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:40.320
Safar.

15
00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:43.260
Interactive stories for
workplace learning teams,

16
00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:47.070
so people practice hard decisions,
instead of just reading about them.

17
00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:48.450
And ZoneSight.

18
00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:51.380
A product I developed that looks
for behavioral evidence

19
00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:53.470
of skills that are hard to measure.

20
00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:55.700
We partnered with a nationwide provider,

21
00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:59.770
and published it at
IEEE EDUCON in 2025.

22
00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:04.130
I built it while I was Chief Innovation
Officer at The Possible Zone,

23
00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:08.450
a workforce-development organization
and youth business incubator in Boston.

24
00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:12.750
If you've got something that needs
building, let's start with a jam session:

25
00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:16.170
your problem, a whiteboard,
and what's possible.
